This project uses this GitHub repo: git@github.com:mondyv/Wheres-The-Brainrot.git
The main branch is: master

Before starting any coding/editing task, always run:
git pull origin master

After finishing any changes, always run:
git add .
git -c user.name="mondyv" -c user.email="limeladzs@gmail.com" commit -m "short clear description of what changed"
git push origin master

Never skip the pull or push step.
Never use force push.
Never use git pull --rebase.
If there are no changes to commit, do not make an empty commit, just say there were no changes.
If there are merge conflicts, stop and explain which files conflict before doing anything.
If push is rejected, run git pull origin master first then push again.

NEVER use git pull --rebase under any circumstances. If you are about to use --rebase, stop and use git pull origin master instead.
